### Express runs on 3000, Spring on 8080. Change this line to switch.
@host = http://localhost:3000

### Create a note
POST {{host}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Buy milk"}

### Get all notes
GET {{host}}/notes

### Get one note
GET {{host}}/notes/1

### Delete a note
DELETE {{host}}/notes/1


### ===== Break-it lab =====

### 1. POST without Content-Type
POST {{host}}/notes

{"text": "no header"}

### 2. POST with broken JSON
POST {{host}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{text: }

### 3. Id that is not a number
GET {{host}}/notes/abc

### 4. Method that does not exist yet
PUT {{host}}/notes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "changed"}

### 5. Remove express.json() in app.js / @RequestBody in NoteController,
###    restart, then run "Create a note" again.


### ===== Step 2 only (database) =====

### 6. Note without text: the database rejects it (text is NOT NULL)
###    Afterwards, try "Get all notes". Is the server still running?
POST {{host}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{}
